@startuml HermesCLIExternalRequests
title hermes-cli: external request / response messages (proposal)
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class "Request envelope" as Request {
  schema_version: integer
  request_id: string
  operation: string
  payload: operation-specific object
}
class "Success response" as Success {
  schema_version: integer
  request_id: string
  operation: string
  status: success
  payload: operation-specific object
}
class "Error response" as Error {
  schema_version: integer
  request_id: string
  operation: string
  status: error
  error.code / error.message
  error.field_errors?: FieldError[]
  error.current_version?: Version
  error.effect?: rejected | committed | unknown
}
package "CLI -> document-service: example payloads" {
  class Authenticate {
    credentials.method: string
    credentials.proof: object (OPEN)
  }
  class UpdateDocument {
    document_id: ID
    title: string
    content: Markdown
    expected_version: Version
  }
  class RespondToInvitation {
    invitation_id: ID
    decision: accept | decline
  }
}
package "document-service -> CLI: example success payloads" {
  class "Authenticate result" as Session {
    user_id: ID
    token: opaque secret
    expires_at: Timestamp
  }
  class "UpdateDocument result" as Write {
    document: Document
    changed: boolean
  }
  class Document {
    id: ID
    workspace_id: ID
    title: string
    content: Markdown
    version: Version
  }
  class "Invitation result" as Invitation {
    invitation.id / workspace_id
    invitation.inviter_id / invitee_id
    invitation.role / status / expires_at
  }
}
Request ..> Authenticate : payload example
Request ..> UpdateDocument : payload example
Request ..> RespondToInvitation : payload example
Success ..> Session : payload example
Success ..> Write : payload example
Success ..> Invitation : payload example
Write *-- Document
Request --> Success : same request_id and operation
Request --> Error : alternative response
note bottom of Request
  Protected requests carry a session token in secure headers/metadata.
  Actor identity comes from the session, not a client actor_id.
  Logical envelopes do not select HTTP/gRPC encoding or endpoints.
end note
legend bottom
  Complete operation catalogue and field definitions: hermes-cli.md.
  Request ID correlates messages; it is not an idempotency key.
  Timeout without response is a local adapter error, not a received Error frame.
  Drafts, editor paths, context.Context and Go errors stay inside the CLI.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml HermesCLIExternalPush
title notification-service -> hermes-cli: public push messages (proposal)
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class "Public message envelope" as Message {
  schema_version: integer
  message_id: ID
  kind: refresh | notice
  type: string
  occurred_at: Timestamp
  delivery: live | backlog
  source_event_id?: ID
  workspace_id?: ID
  target?: TargetRef
  payload: type-specific object
}
class TargetRef {
  type: user | workspace | document | invitation
  id: ID
}
package "Refresh payload examples" {
  class DocumentChanged {
    document_id: ID
    version: Version
  }
  class WorkspaceChanged {
    workspace_id: ID
    version?: Version
  }
}
package "Personal notice payload examples" {
  class WorkspaceInvitationReceived {
    invitation_id: ID
    workspace_id: ID
    role: admin | editor | viewer
  }
  class ProfileChanged {
    changed_fields: username | email []
  }
  class DocumentDeleted {
    document_id: ID
    workspace_id: ID
  }
}
Message o-- TargetRef
Message ..> DocumentChanged : type selects payload
Message ..> WorkspaceChanged : type selects payload
Message ..> WorkspaceInvitationReceived : type selects payload
Message ..> ProfileChanged : type selects payload
Message ..> DocumentDeleted : type selects payload
note bottom of Message
  HNS validates the same opaque token during WebSocket handshake.
  Live fan-out reaches all active recipient connections.
  Backlog goes to one connecting session; coordination/ack/replay OPEN.
  This is a public message, not the internal Kafka event envelope.
end note
note bottom of DocumentDeleted
  Minimal fact only; no openable target and no document contents.
  Other objects are opened through document-service with current access checks.
end note
legend bottom
  Full proposed type catalogue and OPEN controls: hermes-cli.md.
  Stable message IDs, ordering, duplicate suppression and delivery guarantees OPEN.
  No session tokens, credentials, private email values or document bodies.
  Redis settings Pub/Sub is internal to services, not a CLI push frame.
endlegend
@enduml
